                "source": [
                    "# Predictive Analytics and Time Series Forecasting\n",
                    "## Overview\n",
                    "**Advanced predictive modeling and time series forecasting for treasury risk management**\n",
                    "\n",
                    "## Introduction\n",
                    "This notebook provides comprehensive coverage of Predictive Analytics and Time Series Forecasting techniques. It focuses on developing advanced forecasting models to predict treasury cash flows, detect anomalies, and optimize financial decision-making through data-driven insights.\n",
                    "\n",
                    "### Learning Objectives:\n",
                    "- Master time series forecasting techniques for treasury analytics\n",
                    "- Implement machine learning models for cash flow prediction\n",
                    "- Develop anomaly detection algorithms for treasury risk management\n",
                    "- Create automated forecasting pipelines for real-time decision making\n",
                    "- Build comprehensive forecasting dashboards for stakeholders\n",
                    "\n",
                    "### Prerequisites:\n",
                    "- Understanding of statistical forecasting concepts\n",
                    "- Basic knowledge of machine learning algorithms\n",
                    "- Familiarity with Python libraries for time series analysis\n",
                    "\n",
                    "### Step-by-Step Instructions:\n",
                    "1. Load and preprocess treasury time series data\n",
                    "2. Perform exploratory time series analysis\n",
                    "3. Implement ARIMA and Prophet forecasting models\n",
                    "4. Build machine learning models for cash flow prediction\n",
                    "5. Develop anomaly detection using LSTM networks\n",
                    "6. Create forecasting dashboard and automated reports\n",
                    "\n",
                    "### Key Features:\n",
                    "- ✅ Advanced time series forecasting models\n",
                    "- ✅ Machine learning for cash flow prediction\n",
                    "- ✅ LSTM-based anomaly detection\n",
                    "- ✅ Automated forecasting pipelines\n",
                    "- ✅ Interactive visualization tools\n",
                    "- ✅ Attribution support\n"
                ]
            },
            {
                "cell_type": "code",
                "execution_count": None,
                "metadata": {},
                "outputs": [],
                "source": [
                    "import pandas as pd\n",
                    "import numpy as np\n",
                    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
                    "import seaborn as sns\n",
                    "from sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression\n",
                    "from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestRegressor\n",
                    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
                    "\n",
                    "print('🚀 Treasury Analytics Notebook: Predictive Analytics and Time Series Forecasting')\n",
                    "print('✅ Environment ready for advanced treasury forecasting\n')\n",
                    "\n",
                    "# Generate treasury time series data for forecasting\n",
                    "np.random.seed(42)\n",
                    "\n",
                    "def generate_time_series_data(n_samples=500):\n",
                    "    dates = pd.date_range('2024-01-01', periods=n_samples, freq='D')\n",
                    "    # Base cash flow with seasonal patterns\n",
                    "    base_flow = np.random.lognormal(8, 1.5, n_samples)\n",
                    "    # Add seasonal component\n",
                    "    seasonal = 50000 * np.sin(2 * np.pi * np.arange(n_samples) / 365)\n",
                    "    # Add trend\n",
                    "    trend = np.arange(n_samples) * 100
",
 "# Add noise and anomalies\n",
 "noise = np.random.normal(0, 5000, n_samples)\n",
 "anomalies = np.zeros(n_samples)\n",
 "anomalies[::50] = np.random.choice([-20000, 20000], 10)\n",
 "\n",
 "amount = base_flow + seasonal + trend + noise + anomalies\n",
 "\n",
 "data = {\n",
 "    'date': dates,\n",
 "    'cash_flow': amount,\n",
 "    'day_of_week': np.random.choice(['Monday', 'Tuesday', 'Wednesday', 'Thursday', 'Friday', 'Saturday', 'Sunday'], n_samples),\n",
 "    'month': np.random.choice(list(range(1, 13)), n_samples),\n",
 "    'is_weekend': np.random.choice([True, False], n_samples, p=[0.2, 0.8]),\n",
 "    'risk_score': np.random.beta(1, 3, n_samples)\n",
 "}\n",
 "\n",
 "return pd.DataFrame(data)\n",
 "\n",
 "df = generate_time_series_data(365)\n",
 "\n",
 "print('📊 Time Series Data Overview:')\n",
 "print(f\"Date range: {df['date'].min()} to {df['date'].max()}\")\n",
 "print(f\"Total periods: {len(df):,}\")\n",
 "print(f\"Average daily cash flow: ₹{df['cash_flow'].mean():,.0f}\")\n",
 "print(f\"Cash flow volatility: ₹{df['cash_flow'].std():,.0f}\")\n",
 "print(f\"Weekend vs Weekday ratio: {df[df['is_weekend']]['cash_flow'].mean():,.0f} vs {df[~df['is_weekend']]['cash_flow'].mean():,.0f}\\n')\n",
 "\n",
 "print('🔍 Data Structure:')\n",
 "print(df.head(3))\n"
                ]
            },
            {
                "cell_type": "code",
                "execution_count": None,
                "metadata": {},
                "outputs": [],
                "source": [
                    "# Time Series Analysis and Forecasting Section\n",
                    "print('🔬 Time Series Analysis and Forecasting:')\n",
                    "\n",
                    "# Simple linear regression forecast\n",
                    "print('📈 Linear Regression Forecast:')\n",
                    "X = df[['day_of_week']].astype(hash(df['day_of_week'].values))  # Simple encoding\n",
                    "y = df['cash_flow']\n",
                    "model = LinearRegression()\n",
                    "model.fit(X, y)\n",
                    "predictions = model.predict(X)\n",
                    "\n",
                    "# Forecast accuracy calculation\n",
                    "mape = np.mean(np.abs((df['cash_flow'] - predictions) / df['cash_flow'])) * 100\n",
 "print(f\"Model MAPE: {mape:.2f}%\")\n",
 "\n",
 "# Random Forest for cash flow prediction\n",
 "print('🌳 Random Forest Model:')\n",
 "rf_model = RandomForestRegressor(n_estimators=100, random_state=42)\n",
 "rf_model.fit(X, y)\n",
 "rf_predictions = rf_model.predict(X)\n",
 "\n",
 "rf_mape = np.mean(np.abs((df['cash_flow'] - rf_predictions) / df['cash_flow'])) * 100\n",
 "print(f\"Random Forest MAPE: {rf_mape:.2f}%\")\n",
 "\n",
 "# Seasonal decomposition (simplified)\n",
 "print('📊 Seasonal Decomposition:')\n",
 "# Extract seasonal component using moving average\n",
 "window = 7\n",
 "rolling_mean = df['cash_flow'].rolling(window=window, center=True).mean()\n",
 "rolling_std = df['cash_flow'].rolling(window=window, center=True).std()\n",
 "\n",
 "# Plot forecasts\n",
 "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n",
 "plt.plot(df['date'], df['cash_flow'], label='Actual Cash Flow', alpha=0.7)\n",
 "plt.plot(df['date'], predictions, label='Linear Regression Forecast', linewidth=2)\n",
 "plt.plot(df['date'], rf_predictions, label='Random Forest Forecast', linewidth=2)\n",
 "plt.title('Treasury Cash Flow Forecast Comparison')\n",
 "plt.xlabel('Date')\n",
 "plt.ylabel('Cash Flow (₹)')\n",
 "plt.legend()\n",
 "plt.xticks(rotation=45)\n",
 "plt.tight_layout()\n",
 "plt.show()\n",
 "\n",
 "print('🎯 Time Series Forecasting Complete!')\n"
                ]
            }
